<h3 data-start="964" data-end="1034" class="">2. <strong data-start="971" data-end="1034">Was bedeutet â€žPeriode vor dem Kommaâ€œ im p-adischen Kontext?</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1036" data-end="1263" class="">Im p-adischen System ist die Zahl <strong data-start="1070" data-end="1095">nach rechts unendlich</strong>, d.â€¯h. Richtung <strong data-start="1112" data-end="1142">kleiner werdender Potenzen</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8588em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6644em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> mit <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>â†’</mo><mo>âˆ’</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆž</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n \to -\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">â†’</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">âˆ’</span><span class="mord">âˆž</span></span></span></span> (anders als bei reellen Dezimalzahlen). Eine <strong data-start="1222" data-end="1247">Periode vor dem Komma</strong> bedeutet daher:</p>
<ul data-start="1265" data-end="1480">
<li data-start="1265" data-end="1345" class="">
<p data-start="1267" data-end="1345" class="">Es gibt eine <strong data-start="1280" data-end="1311">wiederkehrende Ziffernfolge</strong> in den <strong data-start="1319" data-end="1344">hÃ¶herwertigen Stellen</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1346" data-end="1480" class="">
<p data-start="1348" data-end="1480" class="">In der Baum-Metapher: Ab einer bestimmten Tiefe (oben!) wiederholt sich der Pfad zyklisch â€“ du kehrst zum gleichen Astmuster zurÃ¼ck.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1482" data-end="1704" class="">Das ist analog zur PeriodizitÃ¤t in der <strong data-start="1521" data-end="1565">p-adischen Entwicklung rationaler Zahlen</strong>:<br data-start="1566" data-end="1569">
Jede rationale Zahl hat eine <strong data-start="1598" data-end="1628">eventuell endliche Periode</strong> in ihrer <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span>-adischen Expansion â€“ oft â€žobenâ€œ bei den groÃŸen Exponenten.</p>
<hr data-start="1706" data-end="1709" class="">
<h3 data-start="1711" data-end="1776" class="">3. <strong data-start="1718" data-end="1776">Der Baum als Modell fÃ¼r PrÃ¤zision und Kongruenzklassen</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1778" data-end="1821" class="">In der Topologie der p-adischen Zahlen ist:</p>
<ul data-start="1823" data-end="2065">
<li data-start="1823" data-end="1892" class="">
<p data-start="1825" data-end="1892" class="">Jeder Knoten entspricht einer <strong data-start="1855" data-end="1891">Kongruenzklasse modulo <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8588em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6644em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1893" data-end="1987" class="">
<p data-start="1895" data-end="1987" class="">Die <strong data-start="1899" data-end="1927">Verfeinerung der Klassen</strong> durch kleinere <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span> entspricht dem Hinabsteigen im Baum.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1988" data-end="2065" class="">
<p data-start="1990" data-end="2065" class="">Die Zahl ist also ein <strong data-start="2012" data-end="2064">Pfad durch diese immer feineren Klassenteilungen</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2067" data-end="2252" class="">Eine <strong data-start="2072" data-end="2083">Periode</strong> im Baumpfad bedeutet, dass man sich <strong data-start="2120" data-end="2165">in einem zyklischen Teil des Baums bewegt</strong>, also dass die Zahl modulo <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8588em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6644em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> fÃ¼r wachsendes <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span> einem festen Muster folgt.</p>
<hr data-start="2254" data-end="2257" class="">
<h3 data-start="2259" data-end="2269" class="">Fazit:</h3>
<p data-start="2271" data-end="2432" class=""><strong data-start="2271" data-end="2412">Ja, eine p-adische Zahl mit PeriodizitÃ¤t in den hÃ¶heren Stellen entspricht einem Pfad in einem p-Ã¤ren Baum, der sich zyklisch wiederholt.</strong> Diese Baumstruktur:</p>
<ul data-start="2434" data-end="2658">
<li data-start="2434" data-end="2483" class="">
<p data-start="2436" data-end="2483" class="">Modelliert die Hierarchie der <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span>-Potenzen,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2484" data-end="2543" class="">
<p data-start="2486" data-end="2543" class="">reflektiert die Kongruenzstruktur von <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.975em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">Z</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">p</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2544" data-end="2658" class="">
<p data-start="2546" data-end="2658" class="">erlaubt geometrische oder algorithmische Deutungen (wie in der Automata-Zahlentheorie oder Berkovich-Geometrie).</p>
