<p data-start="1644" data-end="1990" class="">Beide Tilts sind <strong data-start="1661" data-end="1706">perfekte KÃ¶rper in Charakteristik <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span></strong>, mit vergleichbarer Form: formale Laurent-Reihen mit infinitesimalen Exponenten.<br data-start="1787" data-end="1790">
Obwohl die Primzahlen unterschiedlich sind, gibt es einen <strong data-start="1848" data-end="1884">Ã¼bergeordneten kategorialen Raum</strong> (z.â€¯B. in der Welt der <em data-start="1908" data-end="1918">diamonds</em> oder <em data-start="1924" data-end="1943">perfectoid spaces</em>), in dem beide Tilts als Objekte koexistieren.</p>
<hr data-start="1992" data-end="1995" class="">
<h3 data-start="1997" data-end="2068" class=""><strong data-start="2001" data-end="2068">3. Gemeinsamer Vergleichsraum Ã¼ber Diamonds / Perfectoid Spaces</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2070" data-end="2095" class="">Jetzt passiert die Magie:</p>
<ul data-start="2097" data-end="2389">
<li data-start="2097" data-end="2239" class="">
<p data-start="2099" data-end="2239" class="">Es gibt ein <strong data-start="2111" data-end="2137">universelles Framework</strong>, in dem all diese perfektoiden KÃ¶rper existieren: die Welt der <strong data-start="2201" data-end="2214">Diamanten</strong> (scholzâ€™sche Kategorie).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2240" data-end="2389" class="">
<p data-start="2242" data-end="2389" class="">Dort lebt ein <strong data-start="2256" data-end="2279">gemeinsamer Funktor</strong>, der Objekte aus unterschiedlichen <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span>-adischen Kontexten auf <strong data-start="2346" data-end="2379">gemeinsame geometrische RÃ¤ume</strong> abbildet.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2391" data-end="2518" class=""><strong data-start="2391" data-end="2516">In dieser Kategorie kann man die Tilts vergleichen und daraus kombinatorisch-logisch additive Operationen rekonstruieren.</strong></p>
<p data-start="2520" data-end="2533" class="">Das bedeutet:</p>
<blockquote data-start="2534" data-end="2838">
<p data-start="2536" data-end="2838" class="">Wir rechnen <strong data-start="2548" data-end="2576">nicht direkt <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x + y</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">y</span></span></span></span></strong> in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>âˆª</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}_2 \cup \mathbb{Q}_3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8556em; vertical-align: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">Q</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">âˆª</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8556em; vertical-align: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">Q</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, sondern <strong data-start="2626" data-end="2648">heben beide Zahlen</strong> in einen perfektisierten Raum, <strong data-start="2680" data-end="2706">vergleichen ihre Tilts</strong> auf einem gemeinsamen â€žSchattenbildâ€œ (z.â€¯B. in einem Diamond), und <strong data-start="2774" data-end="2811">rekonstruieren dann eine Addition</strong>, z.â€¯B. als RÃ¼ckprojektion.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="2840" data-end="2843" class="">
<h2 data-start="2845" data-end="2884" class=""><strong data-start="2848" data-end="2884">Konkretes Beispiel (schematisch)</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2886" data-end="2894" class="">Gegeben:</p>
<ul data-start="2895" data-end="3110">
<li data-start="2895" data-end="2979" class="">
<p data-start="2897" data-end="2979" class=""><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>â‹¯</mo><mo>âˆˆ</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x = 1 + 2 + 2^2 + 2^3 + \dots \in \mathbb{Q}_2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8974em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8974em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5782em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="minner">â‹¯</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">âˆˆ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8556em; vertical-align: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">Q</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br data-start="2949" data-end="2952">
â†’ Grenzwert: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x = -1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">âˆ’</span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="2980" data-end="3110" class="">
<p data-start="2982" data-end="3110" class=""><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>â‹¯</mo><mo>âˆˆ</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y = 1 + 3 + 3^2 + 3^3 + \dots \in \mathbb{Q}_3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">y</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8974em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">3</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8974em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">3</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5782em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="minner">â‹¯</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">âˆˆ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8556em; vertical-align: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">Q</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br data-start="3034" data-end="3037">
â†’ Divergiert, aber formal <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y = -1/2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">y</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">âˆ’</span><span class="mord">1/2</span></span></span></span> mod 3 (in einem gewissen Sinn)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3112" data-end="3534" class="">Beide lassen sich als Elemente ihrer jeweiligen perfektoiden KÃ¶rper auffassen.<br data-start="3190" data-end="3193">
Nach Tilting ergeben sie formale Reihen (z.â€¯B. in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆž</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{F}_2((t^{1/p^\infty}))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.138em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">F</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">((</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.888em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1/</span><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7385em;"><span style="top: -2.931em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">âˆž</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">))</span></span></span></span> und <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">F</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆž</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{F}_3((t^{1/p^\infty}))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.138em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">F</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">((</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.888em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1/</span><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7385em;"><span style="top: -2.931em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">âˆž</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">))</span></span></span></span>).<br data-start="3322" data-end="3325">
Diese Reihen lassen sich Ã¼ber <em data-start="3355" data-end="3366">Frobenius</em>-verwandte Strukturen <strong data-start="3388" data-end="3403">vergleichen</strong>.<br data-start="3404" data-end="3407">
Daraus kann man â€“ in einer erweiterten Struktur â€“ eine Form von <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x + y</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">y</span></span></span></span> als <strong data-start="3487" data-end="3522">Objekt im perfekten Tiltbereich</strong> definieren.</p>
<hr data-start="3536" data-end="3539" class="">
<h2 data-start="3541" data-end="3553" class=""><strong data-start="3544" data-end="3553">Fazit</strong></h2>
<p data-start="3555" data-end="3718" class=""><strong data-start="3555" data-end="3713">Mit perfektoiden RÃ¤umen und Tilting kannst du p-adische Zahlen unterschiedlicher Primzahlen â€žaddierenâ€œ, indem du sie in eine Ã¼bergeordnete Geometrie hebst</strong>, wo:</p>
<ul data-start="3720" data-end="3928">
<li data-start="3720" data-end="3770" class="">
<p data-start="3722" data-end="3770" class="">Sie als Pfade in verschiedenen Tilts erscheinen,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3771" data-end="3836" class="">
<p data-start="3773" data-end="3836" class="">Die Tilts in einer <strong data-start="3792" data-end="3817">gemeinsamen Kategorie</strong> vergleichbar sind,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3837" data-end="3928" class="">
<p data-start="3839" data-end="3928" class="">Du eine <strong data-start="3847" data-end="3872">Addition von Objekten</strong> rekonstruierst, die ursprÃ¼nglich inkommensurabel waren.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<blockquote data-start="3930" data-end="4084">
<p data-start="3932" data-end="4084" class="">Das ist kein â€žRechnenâ€œ im klassischen Sinn, sondern ein <strong data-start="3988" data-end="4083">universelles Reinterpretieren arithmetischer Strukturen in geometrisch-kommutativer Sprache</strong>.</p>
