<hr data-start="188" data-end="191" class="">
<h2 data-start="193" data-end="245" class=""><strong data-start="196" data-end="245">1. Sind Laurent-Reihen dasselbe wie Polynome?</strong></h2>
<p data-start="247" data-end="271" class=""><strong data-start="247" data-end="271">Nein, aber verwandt.</strong></p>
<ul data-start="273" data-end="754">
<li data-start="273" data-end="419" class="">
<p data-start="275" data-end="295" class="">Ein <strong data-start="279" data-end="290">Polynom</strong> ist:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>â‹¯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t) = a_0 + a_1 t + a_2 t^2 + \dots + a_n t^n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7651em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0141em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="minner">â‹¯</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8644em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7144em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="357" data-end="419" class="">â†’ nur <strong data-start="363" data-end="386">endlich viele Terme</strong>, <strong data-start="388" data-end="418">keine negativen Exponenten</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="421" data-end="609" class="">
<p data-start="423" data-end="450" class="">Eine <strong data-start="428" data-end="445">Laurent-Reihe</strong> ist:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>âˆ‘</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>âˆ’</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆž</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆž</mi></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t) = \sum_{n = -\infty}^{\infty} a_n t^n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.9597em; vertical-align: -1.3083em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.6514em;"><span style="top: -1.9em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span><span class="mrel mtight">=</span><span class="mord mtight">âˆ’</span><span class="mord mtight">âˆž</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">âˆ‘</span></span></span><span style="top: -4.3em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">âˆž</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7144em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="508" data-end="609" class="">â†’ <strong data-start="510" data-end="535">unendlich viele Terme</strong>, <strong data-start="537" data-end="571">auch negative Potenzen erlaubt</strong>, eventuell formal (nicht konvergent).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="611" data-end="754" class="">
<p data-start="613" data-end="666" class="">Eine <strong data-start="618" data-end="633">Potenzreihe</strong> ist wie ein unendliches Polynom:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo>âˆ‘</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆž</mi></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n = 0}^\infty a_n t^n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.9185em; vertical-align: -1.2671em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.6514em;"><span style="top: -1.8829em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span><span class="mrel mtight">=</span><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">âˆ‘</span></span></span><span style="top: -4.3em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">âˆž</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.2671em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7144em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="709" data-end="754" class="">â†’ keine negativen Exponenten, aber unendlich.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="756" data-end="854" class=""><strong data-start="756" data-end="774">Laurent-Reihen</strong> sind also wie â€žPotenzreihen mit Vergangenheitâ€œ (negative Potenzen von <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6151em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span></span>).</p>
<hr data-start="856" data-end="859" class="">
<h2 data-start="861" data-end="912" class=""><strong data-start="864" data-end="912">2. Was ist eine pro-Ã©tale Quotientenbildung?</strong></h2>
<p data-start="914" data-end="1043" class="">Ein <strong data-start="918" data-end="941">pro-Ã©tales Quotient</strong> ist ein struktureller Prozess in der modernen Geometrie, besonders in Scholzeâ€™s Theorie der Diamonds.</p>
<p data-start="1045" data-end="1066" class=""><strong data-start="1045" data-end="1066">Was bedeutet das?</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1068" data-end="1514">
<li data-start="1068" data-end="1176" class="">
<p data-start="1070" data-end="1176" class="">Ã‰tale Morphismen: â€žglatteâ€œ, lokal isomorphe Abbildungen von Schemata. â†’ sie erhalten <strong data-start="1155" data-end="1175">lokale Geometrie</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1177" data-end="1348" class="">
<p data-start="1179" data-end="1348" class=""><strong data-start="1179" data-end="1192">Pro-Ã©tale</strong> bedeutet: inverse Limite (Projektivlimit) von Ã©talen Abbildungen.<br data-start="1258" data-end="1261">
â†’ Man denkt sich <strong data-start="1280" data-end="1319">unendlich viele Ã©tale Ãœberdeckungen</strong>, die â€žimmer genauerâ€œ werden.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1349" data-end="1514" class="">
<p data-start="1351" data-end="1514" class=""><strong data-start="1351" data-end="1373">Quotientenbildung:</strong> Man betrachtet zwei perfekte RÃ¤ume mit einer Ã„quivalenzrelation (z.â€¯B. eine Gruppenwirkung), und bildet dann den Raum der Ã„quivalenzklassen.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1516" data-end="1568" class=""><strong data-start="1516" data-end="1536">Beispiel (grob):</strong><br data-start="1536" data-end="1539">
Ein Diamond entsteht oft als:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>â‹„</mo></msup><mo>:</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mo>âˆ¼</mo><mo fence="true">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>pro-</mtext><mover accent="true"><mtext>e</mtext><mo>ËŠ</mo></mover><mtext>tale</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^\diamond := \left[ \tilde{X} / \sim \right]_{\text{pro-Ã©tale}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7241em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7241em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mbin mtight">â‹„</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.9858em; vertical-align: -0.8358em;"></span><span class="minner"><span class="minner"><span class="mopen delimcenter" style="top: 0em;"><span class="delimsizing size2">[</span></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9202em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span></span><span style="top: -3.6023em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.1667em;"><span class="mord">~</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">/</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">âˆ¼</span><span class="mclose delimcenter" style="top: 0em;"><span class="delimsizing size2">]</span></span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist"><span style="top: -2.0003em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">pro-</span><span class="mord accent mtight"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6944em;"><span style="top: -2.7em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="mord mtight">e</span></span><span style="top: -2.7em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.25em;"><span class="mord mtight">ËŠ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mtight">tale</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8358em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1640" data-end="1721" class="">â†’ also: eine Quotientenstruktur, aber in einem extrem feinen topologischen Sinne.</p>
<hr data-start="1723" data-end="1726" class="">
<h2 data-start="1728" data-end="1764" class=""><strong data-start="1731" data-end="1764">3. Was ist Ã©tale Kohomologie?</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1766" data-end="1960" class=""><strong data-start="1766" data-end="1787">Ã‰tale Kohomologie</strong> ist eine mÃ¤chtige Verallgemeinerung der klassischen topologischen Kohomologie fÃ¼r <strong data-start="1870" data-end="1897">algebraische VarietÃ¤ten</strong>, besonders Ã¼ber <strong data-start="1914" data-end="1959">nicht-algebraisch abgeschlossenen KÃ¶rpern</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="1962" data-end="1989" class=""><strong data-start="1962" data-end="1989">Warum brauchen wir sie?</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1991" data-end="2266">
<li data-start="1991" data-end="2068" class="">
<p data-start="1993" data-end="2068" class="">In der klassischen Topologie definieren wir Kohomologie Ã¼ber offene Mengen.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2069" data-end="2193" class="">
<p data-start="2071" data-end="2193" class="">FÃ¼r algebraische VarietÃ¤ten Ã¼ber <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">F</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{F}_p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.975em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">F</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">p</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}_p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.975em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">Q</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">p</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, etc. gibt es keine sinnvolle "offene Umgebungen".</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2194" data-end="2266" class="">
<p data-start="2196" data-end="2266" class="">Ã‰tale Kohomologie ersetzt offene Mengen durch <strong data-start="2242" data-end="2265">Ã©tale Ãœberdeckungen</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2268" data-end="2279" class=""><strong data-start="2268" data-end="2279">Nutzen:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2280" data-end="2433">
<li data-start="2280" data-end="2348" class="">
<p data-start="2282" data-end="2348" class="">Kann Zahlentheorie (z.â€¯B. Galoisgruppen) mit Geometrie verknÃ¼pfen.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2349" data-end="2433" class="">
<p data-start="2351" data-end="2433" class="">Grundlage fÃ¼r Beweise wie <strong data-start="2377" data-end="2406">Weilvermutungen (Deligne)</strong> und <strong data-start="2411" data-end="2432">ModularitÃ¤tssÃ¤tze</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2435" data-end="2438" class="">
<h2 data-start="2440" data-end="2478" class=""><strong data-start="2443" data-end="2478">4. Was sind Shimura-VarietÃ¤ten?</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2480" data-end="2606" class=""><strong data-start="2480" data-end="2502">Shimura-VarietÃ¤ten</strong> sind hochspezialisierte algebraische VarietÃ¤ten, die <strong data-start="2556" data-end="2600">modulare RÃ¤ume fÃ¼r arithmetische Gruppen</strong> sind.</p>
<p data-start="2608" data-end="2624" class=""><strong data-start="2608" data-end="2624">Kurz gesagt:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2625" data-end="2831">
<li data-start="2625" data-end="2716" class="">
<p data-start="2627" data-end="2716" class="">Sie parametrisieren gewisse Hodge-Strukturen, abelsche VarietÃ¤ten mit Levelstruktur, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2717" data-end="2831" class="">
<p data-start="2719" data-end="2831" class="">Sie sind <strong data-start="2728" data-end="2757">arithmetisch extrem reich</strong> â€“ sie codieren z.â€¯B. Modulsysteme wie elliptische Kurven mit Zusatzdaten.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2833" data-end="2851" class=""><strong data-start="2833" data-end="2851">Warum wichtig?</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2852" data-end="2998">
<li data-start="2852" data-end="2998" class="">
<p data-start="2854" data-end="2998" class="">Sie sind die â€žnatÃ¼rlichen RÃ¤umeâ€œ, auf denen sich <strong data-start="2903" data-end="2924">automorphe Formen</strong>, <strong data-start="2926" data-end="2955">Langlands-Korrespondenzen</strong> und <strong data-start="2960" data-end="2987">p-adische Hodge-Theorie</strong> abspielen.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<blockquote data-start="3000" data-end="3136">
<p data-start="3002" data-end="3136" class="">In der modernen Theorie werden Shimura-VarietÃ¤ten oft als <strong data-start="3060" data-end="3072">Diamonds</strong> formuliert â€“ also mit perfektifizierten, pro-Ã©talen Strukturen.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="3138" data-end="3141" class="">
<h2 data-start="3143" data-end="3182" class=""><strong data-start="3146" data-end="3182">5. Was ist der Cartier-Operator?</strong></h2>
<p data-start="3184" data-end="3310" class="">Der <strong data-start="3188" data-end="3208">Cartier-Operator</strong> ist ein spezieller linearer Operator, der in <strong data-start="3254" data-end="3280">Charakteristik <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span></strong> auf Differenzialformen wirkt.</p>
<p data-start="3312" data-end="3334" class="">Er ist eine Abbildung:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Î©</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>â†’</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Î©</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}: \Omega^1 \to \Omega^1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8641em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Î©</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">â†’</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8641em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Î©</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3376" data-end="3481" class="">die bestimmte Strukturen in der <strong data-start="3408" data-end="3431">de-Rham-Kohomologie</strong> von Schemata oder perfekten KÃ¶rpern kontrolliert.</p>
<p data-start="3483" data-end="3501" class=""><strong data-start="3483" data-end="3501">Eigenschaften:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3502" data-end="3648">
<li data-start="3502" data-end="3553" class="">
<p data-start="3504" data-end="3553" class="">Kommt aus der Theorie der <strong data-start="3530" data-end="3552">Frobenius-Struktur</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3554" data-end="3648" class="">
<p data-start="3556" data-end="3648" class="">Er hilft, die <strong data-start="3570" data-end="3583">p-Torsion</strong>, Kristallstruktur und Verschiebung in Kohomologien zu verstehen.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3650" data-end="3684" class=""><strong data-start="3650" data-end="3684">In Kontext mit Cartier-Moduln:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3685" data-end="3849">
<li data-start="3685" data-end="3756" class="">
<p data-start="3687" data-end="3756" class="">Ein <strong data-start="3691" data-end="3708">Cartier-Modul</strong> ist ein Modul mit Aktion des Cartier-Operators.</p>
